&lt;p&gt;Make sure your recovery email address and phone number are current and controlled by you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Review Recent Sign-In Activity&lt;br&gt;
Look for unfamiliar sign-ins and unexpected account changes. Investigate security alerts that you do not recognize.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check Connected Devices and Applications&lt;br&gt;
Review access granted to devices and applications. Remove access you no longer need or do not recognize.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Avoid Phishing Attempts&lt;br&gt;
Do not disclose passwords or verification codes in response to unexpected messages. Visit Yahoo's official website directly when reviewing account security.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sign Out on Shared Devices&lt;br&gt;
When using a public or shared computer, sign out after finishing and avoid saving your password on that device.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo provides additional advice in its official account security guide. &lt;cite&gt;&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Privacy Protection for Yahoo Mail Users&lt;br&gt;
Email accounts often contain information that users should keep private. Messages may include personal correspondence, financial notifications, receipts, and other sensitive details.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Helpful privacy practices include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep passwords and verification codes private.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Review account recovery information regularly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check email filters and forwarding settings for unfamiliar changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Remove unnecessary connected applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Avoid opening suspicious attachments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use appropriate permissions when sharing documents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Protect saved contact information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Avoid accessing another person's messages without authorization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Privacy deserves particular attention when an account has a long history because older correspondence may contain information that is no longer relevant but still needs protection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Organizing an Established Yahoo Mail Inbox&lt;br&gt;
An organized inbox can improve productivity and make communication easier to manage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create Relevant Folders&lt;br&gt;
Separate messages into useful categories such as personal correspondence, work, receipts, subscriptions, and projects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use Filters Carefully&lt;br&gt;
Filters can help organize incoming email automatically. Review them occasionally to make sure important messages are not being redirected unexpectedly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Archive Useful Messages&lt;br&gt;
Archiving helps reduce inbox clutter while keeping messages available for future reference.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Remove Unwanted Subscriptions&lt;br&gt;
Unsubscribe from newsletters you no longer need when appropriate. Report suspicious messages rather than interacting with them.&lt;/p&gt;

