&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Button with thirty boolean props
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the design-system Slack of any growing company and you will eventually find this message: "hey, does anyone know what &lt;code&gt;isCompactSecondaryGhost&lt;/code&gt; does?" The &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt; started life as a humble little thing. Then someone needed a loading state, so they added &lt;code&gt;isLoading&lt;/code&gt;. Then an icon, so &lt;code&gt;hasIcon&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;iconPosition&lt;/code&gt;. Then a destructive variant, a ghost variant, a compact size, a full-width mode, a tooltip-on-disabled hack. Two years later the type signature is a wall.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Button.tsx (the horror)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ButtonProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isPrimary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isSecondary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isGhost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isDanger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isCompact&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isLarge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isFullWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;hasIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;iconLeft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;iconRight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isDisabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;showTooltipWhenDisabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isPill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isOutlined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...and 15 more, half of which are mutually exclusive&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Nothing about that compiles wrong. &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Button isPrimary isSecondary isGhost /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; typechecks perfectly and renders nonsense. The component has become a configuration language nobody designed on purpose. This article is about the discipline that prevents it: &lt;strong&gt;composition over configuration&lt;/strong&gt;, clear component boundaries, prop design that closes invalid states, &lt;strong&gt;design tokens&lt;/strong&gt;, and how all of it rolls up into a reusable component library, a real design system instead of a junk drawer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📌 &lt;strong&gt;Who this is for:&lt;/strong&gt; You ship features in a React/Vue/Svelte codebase and you have felt the rot, components that fork into copies, props that contradict each other, "don't touch that file" comments. You want the senior-level mental models for keeping a UI codebase healthy as the team and surface area grow. Some component framework experience assumed; the principles are framework-agnostic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The one principle: compose small pieces
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compose small pieces; don't configure giant ones. Every boolean prop you add is a branch inside the component, every slot you expose is a branch you handed to the caller.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The whole article in one line&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;configurable&lt;/strong&gt; component tries to anticipate every use case and exposes a prop for each one. The component owns all the variation, so it grows without bound. A &lt;strong&gt;composable&lt;/strong&gt; component does one small job well and lets callers assemble it with siblings and children to get variation. The complexity moves out to the call site, where it is visible and local, exactly where the person who needs the variation is already standing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the real world&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In tech&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A single molded plastic toy, one fixed shape, no parts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A giant component with 30 props: every new need means re-molding the whole thing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A box of LEGO bricks, small, uniform, snap together&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Small primitives (Box, Text, Stack, Button) you compose into anything&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Want a castle and a spaceship from the same bricks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same primitives compose into a form, a card, a toolbar, no new code in the primitive&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A brick has studs in standard positions so any two fit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Props and tokens are the standard interface that lets pieces snap together predictably&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why composition scales and configuration doesn't.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LEGO won because the &lt;em&gt;interface&lt;/em&gt; between bricks is small and uniform. That is the entire trick. Your primitives should have small, uniform interfaces too, then features are assembled, not authored from scratch each time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The picture: how a UI codebase layers
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A healthy frontend isn't a flat pile of components, it's a layered dependency graph. Lower layers know nothing about higher ones. Tokens don't know about buttons; buttons don't know about the checkout page. Dependencies point one way, down.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" alt="Design tokens flow up into primitives, which compose into reusable components, which compose into features and pages. Ea" width="1574" height="230"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Design tokens flow up into primitives, which compose into reusable components, which compose into features and pages. Each layer depends only on the layer below.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Define tokens&lt;/strong&gt;: Name your raw decisions once: &lt;code&gt;color.brand.500&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;space.4&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;radius.md&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;font.size.lg&lt;/code&gt;. No component hardcodes a hex or a pixel value, they reference tokens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Build primitives on tokens&lt;/strong&gt;: A &lt;code&gt;Box&lt;/code&gt; maps props to token-backed styles. A &lt;code&gt;Stack&lt;/code&gt; lays out children with a token-based gap. Primitives are the only layer that touches raw CSS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Compose reusable components&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Input&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt; are built from primitives. They encode brand decisions (a Button always uses brand color + md radius) but stay generic about content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Assemble features&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;LoginForm&lt;/code&gt; composes &lt;code&gt;Input&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;Stack&lt;/code&gt;. It knows about your domain; the components below it do not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Compose pages&lt;/strong&gt;: Routes wire features together. By the time you reach a page, you are arranging blocks, not writing CSS or fixing a Button.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Theme by swapping tokens&lt;/strong&gt;: Dark mode and white-label brands change token &lt;em&gt;values&lt;/em&gt;, not component code. The whole tree re-themes for free because nothing below references a raw value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Presentational vs container components
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Within the component layer there's a second split worth keeping in your head, even in a hooks-everywhere world. &lt;strong&gt;Presentational&lt;/strong&gt; components take data and callbacks via props and render UI, no data fetching, no global state, no business rules. &lt;strong&gt;Container&lt;/strong&gt; (or "connected") components know &lt;em&gt;where&lt;/em&gt; data comes from, they call hooks, read stores, fire mutations, and hand plain props down to presentational children.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The payoff is testability and reuse. A presentational &lt;code&gt;UserCard({ name, avatarUrl, onFollow })&lt;/code&gt; renders identically in Storybook, in a test, and in three different features, because it has no idea where &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; came from. The container &lt;code&gt;ConnectedUserCard&lt;/code&gt; does the &lt;code&gt;useUser(id)&lt;/code&gt; plumbing and renders &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;UserCard {...user} onFollow={follow} /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Keep the wiring thin and shove all the actual UI into the dumb component. Modern code rarely needs two literal files for this, but the &lt;em&gt;boundary&lt;/em&gt;, "this component fetches, that one only renders", is what keeps things sane.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;strong&gt;Tip:&lt;/strong&gt; Rule of thumb: if a component both calls &lt;code&gt;useQuery&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;useStore&lt;/code&gt; &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; contains real layout/markup, it's doing two jobs. Split the data-fetching shell from the presentational core. The core becomes trivially reusable and your design system can ship it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Composition vs configuration: the trade-offs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Configuration isn't &lt;em&gt;always&lt;/em&gt; wrong, a &lt;code&gt;variant="primary"&lt;/code&gt; enum prop is fine and good. The danger is when configuration is used to bolt on &lt;em&gt;structural&lt;/em&gt; variation that should have been composition. Here's how to tell them apart by their symptoms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Dimension&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Configuration (prop-driven)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Composition (slot/children-driven)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Adding a use case&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Add another prop + an internal branch&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Caller arranges existing pieces, no edit to the component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Symptom of overuse&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Prop explosion; mutually exclusive booleans&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Deep nesting at call sites if primitives are too granular&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Invalid states&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Easy to create (&lt;code&gt;isPrimary isGhost&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Hard to create, structure enforces validity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Who owns complexity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The component (grows without bound)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The call site (local and visible)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Best for&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Finite, enumerable variation (size, color)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Open-ended, structural variation (layout, content)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Failure mode&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A god component nobody dares touch&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Boilerplate if you under-abstract&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Reading the symptoms: when a prop should have been a slot.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Over-propped vs composable: the code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The classic example is a &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt;. The configured version tries to own every layout decision through props. Watch how fast it rots:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Card.tsx, the configured (rotting) version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CardProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;subtitle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;imageUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;imagePosition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;top&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;badgeText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;badgeColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;footerText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;primaryActionLabel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;onPrimaryAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;secondaryActionLabel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;onSecondaryAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;showDivider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;isHighlighted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// every new design = a new prop + a new branch in here&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CardProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isHighlighted&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;card card--hl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imageUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imagePosition&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;top&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;img&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imageUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;badgeText&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;badgeColor&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;badgeText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subtitle&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subtitle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;showDivider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;hr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* ...footer, two actions, image-left branch, etc. */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every design tweak edits this file and adds a branch. Now the composable version: &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt; owns &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; the box (background, radius, shadow, padding, all from tokens) and exposes slots via children and sub-components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Card.tsx, the composable version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Card owns the container styling only. Structure is the caller's job.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;highlighted&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;highlighted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data-highlighted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;highlighted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"card"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Small, focused sub-components, the "compound component" pattern.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"card__header"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"card__body"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Footer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"card__footer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;ProductCard.tsx, composing at the call site&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// The variation lives HERE, visible and local. No edit to Card needed.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ProductCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;highlighted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;featured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;tone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"sale"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Sale&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Heading&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Heading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;img&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imageUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Text&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;tone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"muted"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Footer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"primary"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;buy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Add to cart&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"ghost"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Save&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Footer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Notice what happened. &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt; will never grow another prop for a new layout. A wishlist card, a comparison card, an empty-state card, all of them reuse the same &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt; and arrange different children. And &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt; keeps a single &lt;code&gt;variant&lt;/code&gt; enum instead of ten booleans, because &lt;strong&gt;enums make invalid states unrepresentable&lt;/strong&gt;: you literally cannot pass &lt;code&gt;variant="primary" variant="ghost"&lt;/code&gt;. That is prop design as a safety rail, model the finite axes as enums, the open-ended structure as children.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ &lt;strong&gt;Warning:&lt;/strong&gt; Prop boundary rule: a component's props are its public API. Once teams depend on a prop, removing it is a breaking change. Add props reluctantly, name them for &lt;em&gt;intent&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;tone="danger"&lt;/code&gt;) not implementation (&lt;code&gt;color="#e11"&lt;/code&gt;), and prefer &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt; over a &lt;code&gt;content&lt;/code&gt; prop whenever the slot might hold arbitrary markup.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Design tokens: the source of truth
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;design token&lt;/strong&gt; is a named design decision stored as data, not baked into code. Instead of &lt;code&gt;#d97706&lt;/code&gt; scattered across forty files, you have &lt;code&gt;color.brand.500&lt;/code&gt; defined once. Tokens are what let a design system stay consistent and re-theme without a rewrite. They usually come in two tiers: &lt;strong&gt;primitive tokens&lt;/strong&gt; (the raw palette, &lt;code&gt;purple.500 = #d97706&lt;/code&gt;) and &lt;strong&gt;semantic tokens&lt;/strong&gt; (the meaning, &lt;code&gt;color.action.primary = purple.500&lt;/code&gt;). Components reference &lt;em&gt;semantic&lt;/em&gt; tokens, so you can repoint &lt;code&gt;color.action.primary&lt;/code&gt; to a new shade and every button updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;tokens.ts, semantic on top of primitive&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Primitive tier: raw values, no meaning yet.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;purple500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;#d97706&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;pink500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;#ec4899&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;gray900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;#111827&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;gray50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;#f9fafb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Semantic tier: meaning, mapped to primitives. Components use THESE.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;colorActionPrimary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;purple500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;colorTextDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;gray900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;colorSurface&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;gray50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;spaceSm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;8px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;spaceMd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;16px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;radiusMd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;8px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Dark mode = a different semantic mapping, same primitives + components.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;darkTokens&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;colorTextDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;gray50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;colorSurface&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;gray900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In practice these are emitted as CSS custom properties (&lt;code&gt;--color-action-primary&lt;/code&gt;) so theme switching is a single class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and costs nothing at runtime. Tools like Style Dictionary turn one token source into CSS, JS, iOS, and Android outputs, one decision, every platform. The point isn't the tooling; it's the discipline: &lt;strong&gt;no raw values below the token layer&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


From component library to design system
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;People use "component library" and "design system" interchangeably, but they aren't the same. A &lt;strong&gt;component library&lt;/strong&gt; is the code, the reusable &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Input&lt;/code&gt;. A &lt;strong&gt;design system&lt;/strong&gt; is that library &lt;em&gt;plus&lt;/em&gt; the tokens, the usage guidelines, the accessibility contract, the documentation, and the shared vocabulary between design and engineering. The library is the artifact; the system is the agreement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tokens&lt;/strong&gt;, the single source of design truth (covered above).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Primitives + components&lt;/strong&gt;, composable, token-backed, accessible by default (focus rings, ARIA roles, keyboard handling baked in so feature teams can't forget).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;, live examples (Storybook), prop tables, and "do / don't" guidance. Undocumented components get re-invented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Contribution model&lt;/strong&gt;, how a new component gets proposed, reviewed, and promoted from a feature into the shared library. Without this, everyone forks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Versioning&lt;/strong&gt;, semver on the package so breaking a prop is a deliberate, communicated event, not a surprise on Monday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start smaller than you think. You do not need 80 components on day one. Ship tokens + five primitives + the four or five components every feature actually uses (&lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Input&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Card&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Modal&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Stack&lt;/code&gt;). Let real usage pull the next component into existence, promote it &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; it has been copy-pasted twice, not before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Common mistakes that rot a codebase
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Prop explosion.&lt;/strong&gt; Bolting structural variation onto a component as booleans until it has 30 props and four mutually exclusive ones. Fix: reach for children/slots and the compound-component pattern before adding a prop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Premature abstraction.&lt;/strong&gt; Building a "flexible" generic component for a use case you have exactly once, guessing at the future API. The rule of three: don't extract a shared component until the third real usage shows you the actual shape. Wrong abstractions cost more than duplication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No tokens.&lt;/strong&gt; Hardcoded hex codes and pixel values sprinkled everywhere. Dark mode becomes a multi-week migration and brand consistency is a manual code review. Fix: a token layer from day one, even a tiny one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Copy-paste components.&lt;/strong&gt; "I'll just duplicate &lt;code&gt;UserCard&lt;/code&gt; into &lt;code&gt;AdminCard&lt;/code&gt; and tweak it." Now a bug fix has to be applied in two (then five) places and they drift. Fix: compose the shared core, vary via props/children, and a contribution model so the shared version is the easy path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Mixing data and presentation.&lt;/strong&gt; Components that fetch &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; render can't be reused or tested in isolation. Fix: keep the presentational core dumb and push the wiring to a thin container.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The whole article in nine lines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compose small pieces; don't configure giant ones, every boolean prop is a branch you own forever.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LEGO beats a molded toy: small, uniform interfaces let you build anything without re-molding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Layer the codebase: tokens → primitives → components → features → pages, dependencies pointing down only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Split presentational (renders props) from container (knows where data lives), the dumb core is the reusable one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use enums for finite axes (size, variant) and children/slots for open-ended structure; that makes invalid states unrepresentable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat props as a public API: name for intent, add reluctantly, prefer &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt; over a &lt;code&gt;content&lt;/code&gt; prop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design tokens are named decisions as data, primitive tier for raw values, semantic tier for meaning; no raw values below the token layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A component library is the code; a design system is library + tokens + docs + contribution model + versioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start small and let real usage (the rule of three) pull abstractions into existence, never the other way around.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where to go next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Architecture is one of three pillars of a healthy frontend. Once your components compose cleanly, the next questions are where state lives and how the visual layer is built underneath your tokens.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Continue the track:&lt;/strong&gt; the &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/career-paths/frontend-engineer" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend Engineer path&lt;/a&gt; sequences these senior topics with the fundamentals beneath them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Where data lives:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/state-management-in-frontend-apps" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;State Management in Frontend Apps&lt;/a&gt;, the container side of the presentational/container split, in depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The layer under your tokens:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/css-fundamentals-the-box-model-and-layout" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CSS Fundamentals: The Box Model and Layout&lt;/a&gt;, what your primitives are actually emitting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Practice:&lt;/strong&gt; pick your ugliest god-component and refactor it into a compound component this week. Pull the variation out to the call site and watch the prop list collapse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/component-architecture-and-design-systems" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TheSimplifiedTech&lt;/a&gt;, where this guide is interactive, with in-browser terminal labs and diagrams. Learn cloud and DevOps by doing, no videos.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GSAP is an animation engine, not a component library. That is the first thing Google tells you when you search "gsap animation component library", and it is true: GSAP gives you &lt;code&gt;gsap.to()&lt;/code&gt;, ScrollTrigger and SplitText, and leaves the hero reveal, the pinned gallery and the page transition to you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So a small ecosystem of libraries has grown up that sell or give away finished GSAP components. I run one of them (Made for Award), so read this with that in mind. I have tried to be fair, and I link to every site so you can check the current numbers yourself, because prices and counts change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is how the six I know best compare, and who each one is for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Quick comparison
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Library&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What you get&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Frameworks&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Pricing model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Free tier&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://annnimate.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Annnimate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;~119 UI components: buttons, menus, scroll, sections, shaders&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React, Vue, HTML&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Subscription (quarterly / yearly) + one-time kits&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;16-component starter pack&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://madewithgsap.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Made With GSAP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;~121 JS effects: scroll, mouse, drag, infinite&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Webflow, vanilla JS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Subscription (quarterly / annual)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A few free effects&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://osmo.supply" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Osmo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vault of GSAP/Webflow resources and snippets&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Webflow, vanilla, some React&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Subscription&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Some free resources&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://reactbits.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Bits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Animated React components, part GSAP, part Motion&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Free, open source&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Everything&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://tympanus.net/codrops" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Codrops&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Hundreds of demo tutorials, many on GSAP&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vanilla&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Free&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Everything&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.madeforaward.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Made for Award&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;40 award-style components: scroll, hero, preloader, slider, page transition, WebGL&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React, Next.js&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One-time ($22, lifetime)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;8 free components&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Counts are what each site stated in October 2026. Check the links for today's numbers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Annnimate
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The most "design system" of the group. Components are organised like a UI kit (Buttons, Menus, Scroll, Sections, Shaders), every component ships in React, Vue and plain HTML, and there is an MCP server so Cursor or Claude Code can pull the real source while it writes code. The studio behind it has built for Coca-Cola and Powerade and the polish shows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best for:&lt;/strong&gt; teams on a subscription budget who want a consistent kit across React and Vue, and who like the AI-editor integration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch out for:&lt;/strong&gt; it is a subscription, so the components stop coming when you stop paying. Check the licence for client work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Made With GSAP
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;121 effects and counting, all lightweight JavaScript plus GSAP, with an explicit "no Canvas, no WebGL" rule. The sweet spot is Webflow: effects are packaged so you can paste them into a Webflow project, and the source download covers vanilla sites too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best for:&lt;/strong&gt; Webflow designers and anyone who wants scroll and mouse effects without a build step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch out for:&lt;/strong&gt; no React or Next.js versions, and no 3D or shader work by design. Subscription pricing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Osmo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Osmo is a resource vault from the people behind a well-known Webflow/GSAP studio: snippets, cloneables, utilities and full sections, with a strong Webflow bias and growing framework support. Less a component library than a toolbox you dip into.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best for:&lt;/strong&gt; Webflow-first builders who want the studio's own helpers and patterns.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch out for:&lt;/strong&gt; subscription, and you will still assemble most things yourself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. React Bits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Free and open source. A big catalogue of animated React components (text effects, backgrounds, cursors, cards) with a CLI, where some components use GSAP and others use Motion. Quality varies piece to piece, as you would expect from a community project, but for a landing page you can get far at zero cost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best for:&lt;/strong&gt; React developers who want something free today and are happy to adapt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch out for:&lt;/strong&gt; it is a mix of animation engines, so not everything is "GSAP". Expect to tune timings and clean up for production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Codrops
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not a library, but the original source of most of the effects the libraries sell. Every Codrops demo comes with a tutorial and a GitHub repo, many built on GSAP. The catch is that demos are vanilla and written to teach, not to ship: you port them yourself and you handle cleanup, resize and reduced motion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best for:&lt;/strong&gt; learning how an effect works, and developers who prefer to build their own component from a reference.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch out for:&lt;/strong&gt; licences differ per demo; some assets (fonts, images) are demo-only.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. Made for Award
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is mine. Made for Award is a GSAP animation component library: 40 production-ready React and Next.js components (scroll animations, hero sections, preloaders, sliders, page transitions and WebGL effects), 8 of them free and the rest unlocked by one $22 lifetime purchase. Every component has a live demo you can open full-screen before you sign in, and the source is TypeScript + Tailwind with props for the content, so a slider takes your slides and a hero takes your headline.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The focus is narrower than Annnimate's: not a UI kit, but the specific award-site pieces (pinned scroll scenes, preloaders, smoke and wave page transitions, three.js heroes) that are the hard part of a portfolio or agency site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best for:&lt;/strong&gt; React and Next.js developers building a portfolio, agency or launch site who want award-style motion without a subscription.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch out for:&lt;/strong&gt; React only, no Vue or Webflow versions, and a smaller catalogue than the subscription libraries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How to choose
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Webflow:&lt;/strong&gt; Made With GSAP or Osmo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React + Vue in one kit, subscription is fine:&lt;/strong&gt; Annnimate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero budget:&lt;/strong&gt; React Bits, plus Codrops to learn from, plus the free tier of any of the paid ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React or Next.js, pay once:&lt;/strong&gt; Made for Award.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whichever you pick, the thing that matters more than the library is the setup underneath it: register ScrollTrigger once, create animations inside &lt;code&gt;useGSAP&lt;/code&gt; with a scope, put Lenis on the GSAP ticker, and refresh after fonts and images load. Every library above assumes you have that right, and most "the component is broken" issues are one of those four.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If I missed a library you use, tell me in the comments and I will add it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In Vue, Solid, and Angular, state has a type of its own: &lt;code&gt;Ref&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Accessor&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Signal&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In React, the &lt;code&gt;count&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; is just a &lt;code&gt;number&lt;/code&gt;. Nothing in the type tells you:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;that it re-renders the component,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;that it belongs in the dependency array of an effect,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;that a closure may be holding an old copy of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Those questions are left to you and to lint rules. I wanted the type to answer them, so I built&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://github.com/mm1995tk/react-preprocessor" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;react-preprocessor&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Status: experimental.&lt;/strong&gt; The API is still changing. I am posting this to get feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


What it looks like
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;State is &lt;code&gt;Reactive&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. What is computed from it is &lt;code&gt;Derived&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;reactive&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react-preprocessor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Todos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;reactive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;([]); // Reactive&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
const left = todos.derive((list) =&amp;gt; list.filter((t) =&amp;gt; !t.done).length); // Derived&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

reactive.effect(() =&amp;gt; &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; left`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;);

return (
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;each&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;focus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;derive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
);
};
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;At build time, this is rewritten into plain React:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Todos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setTodos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; left`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTodos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;What the preprocessor wrote for you:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The dependency array&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;[owner, left]&lt;/code&gt;, from what the effect reads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The nested immutable update&lt;/strong&gt;, from &lt;code&gt;todo.focus("done").update(...)&lt;/code&gt;. The item is found by key, not by index,
so the update hits the right item even if the list was reordered in the same batch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The &lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, from the first argument of &lt;code&gt;todos.each&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The rules
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;There is no &lt;code&gt;get&lt;/code&gt;. You cannot pull the value out of a &lt;code&gt;Reactive&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. You derive from it, or put it in JSX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using a reactive value as a plain value (&lt;code&gt;`${count}`&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;if (count)&lt;/code&gt;) is a &lt;strong&gt;build error&lt;/strong&gt; with a code frame.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updates are pure functions: &lt;code&gt;update(old =&amp;gt; next)&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;set(next)&lt;/code&gt; is the shortcut for a constant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nested state is updated through lenses (&lt;code&gt;focus&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;each&lt;/code&gt;). Unions are narrowed with &lt;code&gt;when&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;match&lt;/code&gt;,
and the narrowed value is still writable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The source is valid TypeScript, so your editor, type checker, and formatter work unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it is not
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Not a runtime library.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;Reactive&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; exists only at compile time. The output imports only React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Not a performance tool.&lt;/strong&gt; Memoization is left to the React Compiler, which runs after the preprocessor:
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sugar &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tsx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;↓&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;preprocessor&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;plain&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tsx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;↓&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Compiler&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;optimized&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Low commitment
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Adopt per file.&lt;/strong&gt; Files without the sugar are left as they are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;See the output.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;react-preprocessor print src/Todos.tsx&lt;/code&gt; prints the plain React a file becomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Leave any time.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;react-preprocessor eject src --write&lt;/code&gt; rewrites the project to the plain React it compiles to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It works with Vite, Next.js (Turbopack or webpack), and Babel. It also has a Jotai adapter and an oxlint/ESLint rule.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;In the browser:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://mm1995tk.github.io/react-preprocessor/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;the website&lt;/a&gt; lets you edit the examples and see the plain React they become.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;In a project:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;pnpm add -D react-preprocessor&lt;/code&gt;, then follow the &lt;a href="https://github.com/mm1995tk/react-preprocessor#setup" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;setup in the README&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Feedback wanted
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would like to hear:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does the &lt;code&gt;Reactive&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;Derived&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; split make the code easier to read for you, or harder?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which part of the API feels wrong?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Issues and comments are welcome on &lt;a href="https://github.com/mm1995tk/react-preprocessor" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;. A star helps other people find it.&lt;/p&gt;

